&l;p&g;&l;img class=&q;dam-image shutterstock size-large wp-image-1048758089&q; src=&q;https://specials-images.forbesimg.com/dam/imageserve/1048758089/960×0.jpg?fit=scale&q; data-height=&q;640&q; data-width=&q;960&q;&g; Bitcoin and gold might benefit from a bear market in stocks. Shutterstock 
Stocks have encountered some notable volatility lately, with the benchmark S&a;amp;P 500 Index suffering a correction last month and experiencing further weakness in March. 
The major stock indices – specifically the S&a;amp;P 500 and the Dow Jones Industrial Average – have not fallen in to a bear market yet. 
However, any such decline could potentially cause investors to panic, driving them to safe-haven assets like Bitcoin and gold. 
&l;span&g;&l;/span&g; 
&l;strong&g;Turmoil For Stocks&l;/strong&g; 
The stock market has had a rough ride lately. The Dow Jones Industrial Average (DJIA), for example, fell more than 700 points today after President Donald Trump announced tariffs on Chinese goods, according to &l;a href=&q;https://www.bloomberg.com/news/articles/2018-03-21/asian-stocks-face-mixed-start-dollar-sinks-on-fed-markets-wrap&q; target=&q;_blank&q;&g;Bloomberg&l;/a&g;. 
The S&a;amp;P 500 once again&a;nbsp;fell into negative territory for 2018, after recovering from the correction it suffered in the last few months, &l;a href=&q;https://www.google.com/finance&q; target=&q;_blank&q;&g;Google Finance&l;/a&g; data reveals. 
Thus far, these indices have suffered modest volatility. 
&l;!–donotpaginate–&g; 
However, should these benchmark groups of stocks fall in to a full-fledged bear market, investors could panic, flocking to the perceived safety of assets such as gold and Bitcoin. 
&l;img class=&q;dam-image shutterstock size-large wp-image-1051161689&q; src=&q;https://specials-images.forbesimg.com/dam/imageserve/1051161689/960×0.jpg?fit=scale&q; data-height=&q;640&q; data-width=&q;960&q;&g; Bitcoin could benefit significantly from a bear market in stocks. Shutterstock 
&l;strong&g;Bitcoin&s;s Potential Tailwinds&l;/strong&g; 
Bitcoin&a;nbsp;will likely benefit if stocks suffer a &q;major pullback,&q; stated&a;nbsp;&l;span&g;Tim Enneking,&a;nbsp;&l;/span&g;&l;span&g;managing director of&a;nbsp;&l;/span&g;&l;a href=&q;https://www.crypto-asset-management.com/&q; target=&q;_blank&q; rel=&q;nofollow noopener noreferrer&q; target=&q;_blank&q;&g;Crypto Asset Management&l;/a&g;&l;span&g;.&a;nbsp;&l;/span&g; 
Many market observers are closely watching the relationship between the stock market and Bitcoin, noted&a;nbsp;&l;span&g;Mati Greenspan, senior market analyst for social trading platform&a;nbsp;&l;/span&g;&l;a href=&q;https://www.etoro.com/&q; target=&q;_blank&q; rel=&q;nofollow noopener noreferrer&q; target=&q;_blank&q;&g;eToro&l;/a&g;. 
&q;&l;span style=&q;font-weight: 400&q;&g;So far we haven&s;t seen any flows from the stocks into Bitcoin,&q; he stated, emphasizing that many traders do not believe that the recent declines in stocks constitute a bear market.&q;&a;nbsp;&l;/span&g; 
He emphasized that&a;nbsp;&l;span style=&q;font-weight: 400&q;&g;&q;For now most of the selling has been from institutional investors and bots.&q;&a;nbsp;&l;/span&g; 
Greenspan predicted that if a crisis does materialize,&a;nbsp;&l;span style=&q;font-weight: 400&q;&g;&q;It&s;s the retail investors that you&s;d likely see moving to digital assets.&q;&a;nbsp;&l;/span&g; 
&l;strong&g;&s;Too Early To Tell&s;&l;/strong&g; 
Analyst&a;nbsp;Travis Parker&a;nbsp;offered a differing point of view, stating that &q;&l;span style=&q;font-weight: 400&q;&g;It&s;s a little early to tell how cryptocurrency will respond to a market correction.&q;&l;/span&g; 
&l;!–donotpaginate–&g; 
Cryptocurrency &q;&l;span style=&q;font-weight: 400&q;&g;certainly has some of the advantages of precious metals,&q;&a;nbsp;&l;span&g;said Parker,&a;nbsp;COO of&a;nbsp;&l;/span&g;&l;a href=&q;https://irabitcoin.com/&q; target=&q;_blank&q;&g;IRA Bitcoin LLC&l;/a&g;&l;span&g;.&a;nbsp;&l;/span&g;&l;/span&g;&l;span style=&q;font-weight: 400&q;&g;&q;It is a non-correlated asset that &l;/span&g;&l;i&g;&l;span style=&q;font-weight: 400&q;&g;should&l;/span&g;&l;/i&g;&l;span style=&q;font-weight: 400&q;&g; be resistant to market volatility and may even benefit from a sentiment-based shift to alternative assets,&q; he stated.&a;nbsp;&l;/span&g; 
&l;span style=&q;font-weight: 400&q;&g;&q;However a severe market downturn will put pressure on all highly appreciated assets as investors seek to offset market losses with cryptocurrency gains.&q;&l;/span&g; 
&l;img class=&q;dam-image shutterstock size-large wp-image-1051514888&q; src=&q;https://specials-images.forbesimg.com/dam/imageserve/1051514888/960×0.jpg?fit=scale&q; data-height=&q;640&q; data-width=&q;960&q;&g; Gold could easily benefit should stocks suffer notable losses. Shutterstock 
&l;strong&g;Gold&s;s Potential Gains&l;/strong&g; 
Should stocks push lower, gold could certainly benefit, noted analysts. 
Not only is the precious metal a more effective safe-haven asset than bonds, but it is also&a;nbsp;a &q;&l;span style=&q;font-weight: 400&q;&g;non-correlated asset,&q;&a;nbsp;said&a;nbsp;&l;/span&g;Ron Smith, director of trading at &l;a href=&q;https://gsiexchange.com/&q; target=&q;_blank&q;&g;GSI Exchange&l;/a&g;. 
Greenspan offered similar input, stating that &q;&l;span style=&q;font-weight: 400&q;&g;Gold should act as a good indicator of safe haven sentiment.&q;&l;/span&g; 
&l;span style=&q;font-weight: 400&q;&g;&q;If things do get ugly we could see it spike,&q; he added.&a;nbsp;&l;/span&g; 
Gold may have a few other advantages over bitcoin, emphasized&a;nbsp;Oliver Isaacs, blockchain investor and advisor. 
Bitcoin is relatively new, having existed for less than a decade. 
&l;!–donotpaginate–&g; 
In contrast, &q;&l;span style=&q;font-weight: 400&q;&g;gold has 10,000 years of monetary history behind it, and is universally accepted,&q; Isaacs noted.&a;nbsp;&l;/span&g; 
Further, gold benefits from a wide range of hedging products, for example options and futures, he stated. 
Finally, he emphasized that gold is&a;nbsp;&q;&l;span style=&q;font-weight: 400&q;&g;the go-to standard to hedge against potential downside.&q;&l;/span&g; 
